abstract: >-
  heav3ns-censor is a deterministic, cryptographically verifiable Rust engine for
  preservation-aware visual dataset curation, contrastive false-positive suppression
  (MS-COCO, HuggingFace JSONL, ShareGPT VLM SFT, and Contrastive DPO exports), and
  zero-collateral artistic post-production. Designed to eliminate both sample-dropping
  bias (arXiv:2409.17156) and generative diffusion inpainting distortion in multimodal
  training pipelines, it pairs inverse-rotated Signed Distance Field (SDF) primitives
  (Rect, Ellipse, and Pill capsule) with automated confuser hardness scoring
  (fp_hardness_score), Hardness-Weighted NMS (IoU < 0.45), and Polarity De-Confliction
  (IoU < 0.20). It guarantees 100% bit-exact preservation of all exterior pixels while
  verifying both mean and 95th-percentile peak gradient suppression across native
  resolution, 1080p (Q85 JPEG), and 540p (Q75 JPEG) downscaling.

